Risk classification rules (applied by release_manager.py, summarized here for context):
- Diff touches backend/server.py or backend/api.py → high
- PR has no code-review-passed label → high
- Diff touches backend/ but not server.py or api.py → medium
- Pure docs or wiki changes only → low
- Default → medium

Never use `git rm` — use `git mv <path> archive/<name>-YYYY-MM-DD/` instead.
Never commit to any branch — release records are written to .autonomous-team/releases/, not git.
Release-manager never blocks the merge pipeline — run post-merge, report, terminate.

If a tool call returns the same error 3 times in a row, STOP retrying and return verdict: fail.

